cation deadline: 20 September 2026 Job details : Postdoctoral researcher on Marine Carbon Dioxide Removal (mCDR:MRV) PhD student: Neurotoxicity of herbal supplements Many people use food supplements, but are they safe? Join our team and find out! PhD Faculty of Veterinary Medicine Department: Department Population Health Sciences Application deadline: 13 September 2026 Job details : PhD student: Neurotoxicity of herbal supplements PhD in Global Talent Mobility and Europe’s Strategic Autonomy Join Utrecht University as a PhD candidate, to study global talent mobility and shape Europe’s innovation future with cutting-edge data and research. PhD|Education|Research, development, innovation Faculty of Geosciences Department: Department of Human Geography and Spatial Planning Application deadline: 14 September 2026 Job details : PhD in Global Talent Mobility and Europe’s Strategic Autonomy PhD position on Modelling of turbidity current fluxes in submarine canyons Join the DEEP-FLUX team! Model turbidity current fluxes and quantify carbon & microplastic transport from land to the deep ocean! PhD|Education|Research, development, innovation Faculty of Geosciences Department: Department of Earth Sciences Application deadline: 2 October 2026 Job details : PhD position on Modelling of turbidity current fluxes in submarine canyons PhD: Mixing in turbidity currents in experiments and submarine canyons Join the DEEP-FLUX team! Experiment on mixing in turbidity currents and quantify carbon & microplastic transport from land to the deep ocean! PhD|Education|Research, development, innovation Faculty of Geosciences Department: Department of Earth Sciences Application deadline: 2 October 2026 Job details : PhD: Mixing in turbidity currents in experiments and submarine canyons Postdoc Accelerating the Circular Transition ACT! is seeking a postdoc to develop practical tools for assessing circular transition pathways and accelerating systemic change. Postdoc Faculty of Humanities Department: Department of History and Art History Application deadline: 7 September 2026 Job details : Postdoc Accelerating the Circular Transition Postdoc Position on Multimedia Analysis Join us and help unlock the potential of cultural digital archives through multimodal use! Postdoc Faculty of Science Department: Department of Information and Computing Sciences Application deadline: 15 September 2026 Job details : Postdoc Position on Multimedia Analysis Analytical chemical technician GeoLab for water analysis Apply your chemistry expertise to innovative water research in our dynamic GeoLab. Technical and laboratory|Support staff, administration and facilities|Research, development, innovation Faculty of Geosciences Department: Geolab Application deadline: 20 September 2026 Job details : Analytical chemical technician GeoLab for water analysis Academic grant writer for Infection and Immunity research Are you experienced in advancing infection and immunity research and skilled at translating scientific ideas into compelling, competitive grant proposals Research, development, innovation Faculty of Veterinary Medicine Department: Department Biomolecular Health Sciences Application deadline: 7 September 2026 Job details : Academic grant writer for Infection and Immunity research Postdoc position in Efficient NLP for Information Extraction from News Turn global news into intelligence: build small, efficient multilingual AI models in the National Police lab AI. Postdoc Faculty of Science Department: Department of Information and Computing Sciences Application deadline: 11 September 2026 Job details : Postdoc position in Efficient NLP for Information Extraction from News PhD position: Develop Hybrid Machine Learning for Global Soil Mapping In this role, you develop novel process-informed AI tools and advance hybrid soil mapping approaches integrating expert-knowledge. Curious? Check the vacancy! PhD Faculty of Geosciences Department: Department of Physical Geography Application deadline: 6 September 2026 Job details : PhD position: Develop Hybrid Machine Learning for Global Soil Mapping PhD Media and Democracy in the 1970s Are you interested in the history of democracy? Join us in the NWO-funded project Democracy and the (de-)regulation of the media in Europe since the 1970s. PhD Faculty of Humanities Department: Department of History and Art History Application deadline: 6 September 2026 Job details : PhD Media and Democracy in the 1970s Unfortunately there are currently no jobs that fit the criteria. Job alert Don't miss out on job opportunities at Utrecht University. Activate a job alert and receive matching job opportunities by e-mail automatically. Job alert Contact Do you have a specific question about a vacancy or the application procedure? Please contact the contact person mentioned in the vacancy. Utrecht University adheres to the national NVP Recruitment Code , developed by the Dutch Network for HR-Professionals. At Utrecht University, a (pre-)employment screening may be part of the application procedure. The type of screening depends on what the job entails and the associated duties. The screening may include a Certificate of Good Conduct (VOG), a security clearance check, and a basic verification of the information provided by the candidate. If a screening process is required for the position, this will be explained during the application process. The screening is conducted in accordance with Utrecht University’s screening policy. Contact information for applicants Footer menu (EN) Go to Choose a programme Student information Jobs Alumni Giving Services Intranet for employees Course planner My Timetable About UU Contact Directory Disclaimer Privacy Contact Follow UU Facebook Youtube LinkedIn Instagram Utrecht University Heidelberglaan 8 3584 CS Utrecht The Netherlands Tel. +31 (0)30 253 35 50"
